\description{
Bags (baga) are the subdivisions of soums; there are about 1,650 of them.
Their codes and names are built in (see \code{mn_codes("bag")}), but \strong{their
boundaries are not openly published}: the National Statistics Office of
Mongolia (NSO) shares them on request. Once you have a bag boundary file,
\code{mn_bags()} and every other function in the package can use it.
}
\section{Getting bag boundaries}{

Write to NSO (\href{mailto:international@nso.mn}{international@nso.mn}) and ask for the bag boundaries as a
shapefile or GeoPackage, with each bag's NSO code. Then either pass the
file to \code{mn_bags(path = ...)}, or register it once per session with
\code{options(mongolmaps.bags_path = "path/to/bags.gpkg")} (put that line in
your \code{.Rprofile} to make it permanent). Registered bags are also returned
by \code{mn_admin("bag")} and used by \code{\link[=mn_join]{mn_join()}}.

\code{mn_read_bags()} checks the file: every bag must have a known code and
sit inside its soum.
}

